    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1286">

                <pb facs="1264" n="1254" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5–449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Strong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-04T18:00:00+08:00">May 4, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 4—2:12 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>175. [To Nanking:] View conditions stated my telegram 135 to Nanking, 42 OffEmb
                    Canton, 173 Department today,<anchor n="78" xml:id="d1286-f1"/> plus future lack
                    transport except in final emergency, ConGen in agreement with ComNav despatch
                    May 2, quietly by word mouth, advised all non-Asiatics, plus Filipinos, May 12
                    was deadline for normal naval transportation <pb facs="1265" n="1255"
                        xml:id="pg1255"/> to Japan, Hong Kong and advised those not intending remain
                    regardless to take advantage current offers.</p>
                <p>Twenty-one Americans expected leave May 5 and 6 on US naval vessels for Japan,
                    Hong Kong. Anticipate 10 will seek passage later date, leaving approximately 50
                    here. Only few persons of other nationalities leaving.</p>
                <p>Following departure vessels, will report names Americans destined US.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 137, OffEmb Canton 44, Department 175.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Strong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
